1,116.85,114.31,116.09,1030100]],"about":{"what":"CarMax Inc (KMX). This chart runs from Feb 11, 2021 to Jun 21, 2021.","setup":"The stock rose about 51% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 5 weeks, peaking at $136.54 and pulling back 10% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On May 3, 2021 it closed at $136.94, its first close above the base high of $136.54. Volume that day was 1.3M shares, 1.96x the prior 10-day average of 686K. It didn't hold. By May 10, 2021 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $116.09.","lesson":"This is an example of a failed breakout where everything looked right, volume included, and the stock fell back anyway. It happens. This is why traders cut losses fast instead of hoping."}}